## 3. Start server

Do **not** rerun clone/venv. This downloads `Qwen/Qwen3-8B` from Hugging Face into `/kaggle/working/models` on first run.

```python
import os, subprocess, pathlib

os.environ["JAX_COMPILATION_CACHE_DIR"] = "/kaggle/working/jit_cache"
pathlib.Path("/kaggle/working/models").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
pathlib.Path("/kaggle/working/logs").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)

cmd = [
    "/kaggle/working/sglang-env/bin/python", "-u", "-m", "sgl_jax.launch_server",
    "--model-path", "Qwen/Qwen3-8B",
    "--trust-remote-code",
    "--tp-size", "8",
    "--device", "tpu",
    "--mem-fraction-static", "0.8",
    "--chunked-prefill-size", "2048",
    "--download-dir", "/kaggle/working/models",
    "--dtype", "bfloat16",
    "--max-running-requests", "32",
    "--page-size", "128",
    "--host", "0.0.0.0",
    "--port", "30000",
]

log = open("/kaggle/working/logs/sglang.log", "w")
proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
print("pid", proc.pid)
```

First start compiles JAX graphs (`EXTEND` then `DECODE` precompile). Wait. Do not start a second server.

Use a local path after the first download if this folder exists:

```text
/kaggle/working/models/Qwen/Qwen3-8B
```

