## 4. Wait until ready

```python
import requests, time
from pathlib import Path

for i in range(90):
    try:
        r = requests.get("http://127.0.0.1:30000/v1/models", timeout=2)
        if r.ok:
            print("ready", r.json())
            break
    except Exception:
        if i % 10 == 0:
            print("waiting", i)
            p = Path("/kaggle/working/logs/sglang.log")
            if p.exists():
                print(p.read_text()[-800:])
        time.sleep(10)
else:
    raise RuntimeError("server did not start; check /kaggle/working/logs/sglang.log")
```

Ready looks like:

```text
ready {'object': 'list', 'data': [{'id': 'Qwen/Qwen3-8B', ... 'max_model_len': 40960}]}
```

Check log only:

